Hello [~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] [~accountid:6270f0bd807e0000691b79bb] [~accountid:712020:5ee0b1d5-3b9b-4a48-826c-fce4ef2d1492] - thank you all for the productive call earlier today!

To summarised the main takes from the call:

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Polygons based tracking (pick up - drop off metrics):*

# Privacy will focus on the assessment of the polygons functionality; Information provided by LCM in this [doc |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vI-mcMNzYYI2Tg2Fsa7hzoxtBQAEcJdc_3XR-ARU-B4/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.k02nzca1ge4j]allows privacy to run an internal assessment to confirm that its possible not to rely on consent; Preliminary ETA to complete the assessment - two weeks (by 31st of January).
# Our current privacy notices for passengers include wording which already covers the use of pick up and drop off locations for marketing personalisation; *no need to update our privacy notices.*
# No cross-vertical exchange of data/cross-promo is happening - the current initiative only concerns Rides.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Live-location based tracking:*

# Privacy will be able to ad hoc assist with the:
## review of comms to encourage users opt-in consent (email&push); privacy regulation compliant wording must be included;
## review of updates to the “Travelling” category of comms. Preliminary agreed that “Travelling” category of comms will only encompass live location tracking cases. Polygons based tracking can be based under another category, i.e. “promotions and tips”.
# Preliminary position of privacy - consent continues to be the only appropriate lawful basis to use live location for marketing personalisation.
# Privacy responded in comments left in [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vI-mcMNzYYI2Tg2Fsa7hzoxtBQAEcJdc_3XR-ARU-B4/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.k02nzca1ge4j|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vI-mcMNzYYI2Tg2Fsa7hzoxtBQAEcJdc_3XR-ARU-B4/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.k02nzca1ge4j|smart-link] and clarified its concerns re/ ensuring that metrics used by the LCM do not concern any sensitive data (i.e. marking and tracking hospital locations and recommend “Assist” category).
# *No personalisation based on live location is happeneing at the moment.* LCM will keep privacy updates of any specific plans to go live with the live-location personalisaton use cases.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
[I|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/corelocation/monitoring-the-user-s-proximity-to-geographic-regions][*OS geofencing*|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/corelocation/monitoring-the-user-s-proximity-to-geographic-regions] *by the LCM to target our users with geo-specific comms (specifically - in airports):*

# Privacy will internally align if this was previously raised. Privacy compliance and audit trail have to be ensured -  I.e. whether this constitutes geolocation data and how this is contractually managed between Bolt / Apple. 
# Privacy will reach out for additional clarifications if needed.
{panel}

Let me know if you would like to highlight other points from the agenda!

Hi [~accountid:5b7beae8ed4f842a6ddb4713] - I note that the phone number on the account was changed twice on 18 and 19 December. As a result, it has occurred to me that if we have been sending follow-up questions to the requestor via the Bolt app, they may not have been receiving them (on the basis that they may no longer have access to the account).

I therefore have the following suggestions as to immediate next steps:

# Can you please check whether the phone number changes both took place *_after_* the requestor sent their last message to us? If so, can we be confident that this issue is now resolved (i.e., that the incorrect phone number has been removed from the account)?
## Based on this, please proceed with either Option A or Option B below.
# *Option A:* If the requestor’s phone number has been removed from the account (i.e., we are confident that the issue has been resolved):
## Please reach out to the requestor via their phone number (i.e., the phone number that was on the account at the time they issued their complaint - not one of the newer phone numbers resulting from the changes made on 18/19 December), rather than via in-app or email, and send the below:
{color:#4c9aff}_Hello,_{color}
{color:#4c9aff}_We write in relation to your request to remove your phone number from another individual’s Bolt account, which we received on 18 December 2024. We would like to confirm that your phone number has been removed from the Bolt account. If you continue to experience any issues in this regard, or have any further questions, please let us know._{color}
{color:#4c9aff}_Yours sincerely,_{color}
{color:#4c9aff}_Bolt_{color}
# *Option B*: If *_by Monday afternoon (not before)_* we still have reason to believe that this issue is ongoing (i.e., that the requestor’s phone number is still on the account), or we are in any way unsure:
## Please reach out to the requestor via their phone number (i.e., the phone number that was on the account at the time they issued their complaint - not one of the newer phone numbers resulting from the changes made on 18/19 December), rather than via in-app or email, and send the below:
{color:#4c9aff}_Hello,_{color}
{color:#4c9aff}_We write in relation to your request to remove your phone number from another individual’s Bolt account, which we received on 18 December 2024. We are writing to inform you that we require additional time to fulfil your request as we have experienced technical difficulties in resolving this matter. Under relevant data protection legislation, we are permitted to extend the deadline for response by up to an additional two months, which we have determined to be necessary in this instance. We apologise for any inconvenience caused by this extension.  We are committed to providing you with a response to your request as soon as possible. If you have any questions, please let us know._{color}
{color:#4c9aff}_Yours sincerely,_{color}
{color:#4c9aff}_Bolt_{color}

