Hi [~accountid:712020:61ca3c26-7f48-41c2-aa17-30a61b99b569] - comments are as follows:

* If some of these cases were reported to the police, do we have any visibility on whether they are part of an *_ongoing_* police investigation (i.e., have the police notified us that they closed their investigation)? If any of these cases are the subject of an ongoing police investigation, we should +*not*+ be sharing them as part of the DSAR response (even if the driver claims to already be aware).
* If we can be reasonably sure that the case is not part of an ongoing investigation, we can provide them provided that they are _heavily_ redacted. In other words, we should be removing things like:
** Dates / times / any information about the trip like pickup and destination (as this could be used to identify the passenger);
** Any information about third parties (e.g., I see one complaint concerns allegations of raping a young girl - we should redact all of the information about the young girl, as well as anything generally sensitive from this);
** Details of any Bolt employees; 
** Videos taken by the riders in which you can clearly see the rider;
** Internal notes left by Bolt employees on the cases (unless they are innocuous); and
** Anything that is not clearly the driver’s personal data.
* Before sending out the data, please run the redacted copies past me so that I can review.
* Re Zendesk / driver complaints, if we still technically have them on file and don’t have clear grounds for withholding them, IMO we should still provide them (after applying appropriate redactions).

