I've investigated a bit, and it looks like that account hijacking is happened because of a phishing from a Driver account. The Rider reached us from account [240847313|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/240847313/overview?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FLondon], saying his [previous account|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/96417014/sessions?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] with same email got hacked. On [login session page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/96417014/sessions?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] of the original account we see suspicious device logged in on Sept, 18 (8d2f4638a79d13c3). Then, a fraudster using this suspicious session made phone number change on account to {{+447706610217 => +447366853380}}
Using new phone number to sign-in, various [fraudulent orders|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_timestamp%22%3A1731667301%2C%22end_timestamp%22%3A1731797999%2C%22all_order_try_states%22%3Afalse%2C%22user_id%22%3A96417014%7D%7D] were made using user's payment methods. For me it's not clear if funds were authorized because 3DS was required. User was trying to get back into his account, and it leaded to registering a new one. 

Looking into when fraudulent session (device 8d2f4638a79d13c3) appeared the first time - it was during the order. By logs in mixpanel, at this time, [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/1260413?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] (1260413) accepted an order and then declined. In Driver comments in admin-panel there are bunch of reports on Sept, 18 related to fishing from that Driver account. So it looks like fraudster used fishing to get into user's account.

